Subject: [PATCH 3/3] media: cam-cci: reject file ioctls with ENOTTY

The CCI file-operation wrappers intentionally pass NULL to the subdev
handler instead of forwarding userspace arguments containing private CCI
pointers. The NULL-argument path currently returns zero, making unsupported
V4L2 ioctls appear successful without filling their output structures.

In particular, VIDIOC_ENUMINPUT can succeed for every index, causing
GStreamer's V4L2 device discovery to enumerate indefinitely and accumulate
objects, including when discovery is triggered by Chatty/libpurple.

Return -ENOTTY for NULL arguments to reject file ioctls while keeping the
wrappers' NULL forwarding and private CCI pointers inaccessible through
this userspace path. Leave the valid-argument handler unchanged.

Experimental: not yet built or validated on hardware.

---
 techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_cci/cam_cci_dev.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_cci/cam_cci_dev.c b/techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_cci/cam_cci_dev.c
index c949608d183e..313959e30bdb 100644
--- a/techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_cci/cam_cci_dev.c
+++ b/techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_cci/cam_cci_dev.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 
 	if (arg == NULL) {
 		CAM_ERR(CAM_CCI, "Invalid Args");
-		return rc;
+		return -ENOTTY;
 	}
 
 	switch (cmd) {
